# Scalestorm Summoner: the power check is made as the trigger resolves, not when it triggers (it is not an intervening "if"). With no other creature the
# Summoner is a 3/3 and the trigger is on the stack; in response Bot1 casts Giant Growth on it, making it a 6/6, a creature with power 4 or greater, so the
# resolving trigger creates the Dinosaur.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Scalestorm Summoner
Giant Growth
Forest
Forest x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x24

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Scalestorm Summoner.Cast
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Scalestorm Summoner > Bot2)
? Stack.Count = 1
? Bot1.Battlefield.Scalestorm Summoner.Power = 3
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Giant Growth.Cast(Scalestorm Summoner)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Scalestorm Summoner.Power = 6
? Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 5
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Stack.Count = 0

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 6
Bot1.Battlefield.Dinosaur Token.Power = 3
